{
  "title": "Recipe edit: a failed load shows an empty, unsavable form",
  "description": "Web: EditRecipePage.tsx:87 gates the load-error screen on form.error() && loading(), but the finally block (47) always sets loading false, so it never shows. \
The page renders an empty RecipeForm (96) with the error inside it, and submitting throws 'Cannot update a recipe before loading its version' (utils/recipeFormState.ts:250-251). \
Related web state: one error slot covers load, upload and save (uploadPhotoFile clears it at recipeFormState.ts:163, wiping a save error); saving and uploading are independent flags, so Save works mid-upload; the page loads only in onMount (51), so a route id change doesn't reload. iOS (RecipeFormViewModel.swift:308-379, RecipeFormView.swift:77-113): a failed load leaves an empty form with the error, no retry, and Save disabled because expectedVersionId is nil. \
Only isSaving disables the form, so when not resuming a draft, anything typed before the load returns is replaced (loadRecipe, 339). \
One error for load, save and photo upload. \
Want on both clients: an explicit load state (loading / failed with retry / loaded), the form only shown once loaded, and load errors kept separate from save/upload errors. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
